    "text": "A six faced die is biased such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>P</mi></math>(a prime number)<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>P</mi></math>(a composite number)<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math> be a random variable that counts the number of times one gets a perfect square on some throws of this die. If the die is thrown twice, then the mean of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math> is",
